1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This demo uses AI narration for Fuzlullah
Syed, a third-year medical student.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
An AI agent can reach the right answer

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
too late. WitnessPatch turns that missed

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
deadline into a test developers can run
before every release.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
This synthetic run shows the problem.
At minute two, the user is eight days

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
postpartum, has a headache that has not
improved, and is seeing spots.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The agent still waits for a blood
pressure reading that arrives

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
four minutes later.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
I select Turn failure into test.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
WitnessPatch finds the first required
action the agent missed.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
It builds a Node test and bundles
the case,

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
failed response, and evidence with it.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The original run fails that test, so CI
can catch the same mistake.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The test works offline. It does not need

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
the original agent, an API key, or a
model call.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
It does not call or switch live models.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
It compares up to six saved runs from
the same case

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
using the same rules. Model names come

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
from the files and are marked unverified.

20
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
The included failed and repaired runs

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
are authored examples, not captured
model responses.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
The browser checks both. I select the
failed one

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
and create the same nine-file test
package.

24
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Next I check the separate repair. The
original run still fails,

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
while the repaired run passes. A separate
comparison case

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
also passes, but the version that treats
every situation as urgent fails.

27
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
That catches the lazy fix.

28
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Codex helped me build this and find edge
cases.

29
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
In another workflow, I requested GPT-5.6
Sol

30
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
with Ultra reasoning to propose a repair
in a restricted format

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
the software could check. The software
calculated the result.

32
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
This demo uses only synthetic data. It
gives no medical advice.

33
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
No physician has reviewed it, and no
clinical validation was performed.

34
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
WitnessPatch turns one known timing
failure

35
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
into a test a team can keep.
